WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.550
(mellow electronic music)

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.420
- [Narrator] Shanghai is
home to one of the world's

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.370
richest collections of Art Deco buildings.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.340
The city's signature style saw

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.360
its heyday in the 1930s
and epitomized luxury.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.230
It grew increasingly popular with

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.560
the rise of cinema and Hollywood films,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.980
sparking a widespread hunger for the same

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.543
glamorous buildings moviegoers
saw on the silver screen.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.960
- [Announcer] This Great Big
Story was made possible by

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.798
Fairmont, an Accor Hotel experience.

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:33.860
(mellow electronic music)

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:35.890
- [Narrator] Art Deco is
a style of visual arts

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:37.300
that influenced everything from

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.970
architecture to everyday objects.

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.200
Its trademarks are geometric forms,

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.623
linear shapes and narrow windows.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:48.790
A great example is the Grand Theatre.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:51.120
Built in 1928, the Theatre was

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.510
frequented by Shanghai's glitterati,

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:55.840
and features a sophisticated combination

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.370
of modernist and traditional elements.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:01.800
The Theatre boasts a beautiful
modernist Art Deco facade

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:04.663
with its stern horizontal
and vertical lines.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:09.470
Meanwhile, its classical
red and gold interiors

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:12.543
are reminiscent of styles
from Rome or Florence.

00:01:14.653 --> 00:01:16.310
One of the most notorious buildings from

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.170
this golden age of
cinema is the Paramount.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:23.520
Built in 1933, it was the most
glamorous ballroom in town,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.870
and a favorite gathering for

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.140
starlets, tycoons, and gangsters.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.460
Its huge circular tower, with
its avant-garde lighting,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:33.330
was an ambitious and revolutionary

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.240
design element at the time,

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.940
pushing the traditional architectural

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.313
boundaries of 1930’s Shanghai.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.240
Today, Shanghai is widely known
for its futuristic skyline;

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.690
but nestled in between
is a trove of treasures

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.153
of the world's finest
examples of Art Deco.

00:01:57.529 --> 00:02:01.029
(chiming electronic note)

